|* Post-layout sampler_core: the WHOLE composed cell -- four skewed rings,
|* four output buffers, the three-xor2 combining tree, AND all six
|* sampler_dff instances (raw_bit, raw_valid, ring_bit1-4) -- extracted FLAT
|* from ONE `klt extract --parasitics` run over the now DRC-clean, klt
|* lvs-MATCHING layout/sampler_core/sampler_core.gds (264/264 devices,
|* 152/152 nets against design/sampler_core.spice's own .subckt
|* sampler_core, PR #113; extracted as layout/pex-sampler-core/README.md
|* documents, PR #114).
|*
|* Purpose (issue #22's own DR-0008-named follow-up, "sampler_core scope"):
|* every prior sampler_dff-family post-layout deck in this repo
|* (sim/post-layout-sampler-dff/, sim/post-layout-sampler-dff-assembled/)
|* drives ONE isolated sampler_dff instance from an ideal PWL `d` source --
|* never the six-instance fan-out design/sampler_core.spice actually wires,
|* and never a real (not ideal-PWL) input edge. This deck is the first to
|* close both gaps at once: xarr below is the real assembled
|* array-plus-sampler-bank, so each sampler's own `d` pin sees the real,
|* buffer-loaded, post-layout-slowed ring/combining-tree waveform sim/
|* post-layout-ro-array-core/ characterizes -- not a synthetic edge -- and
|* clock-distribution skew across all six instances' own shared `clk` fan-out
|* is present for the first time too. DR-0008's own words: "the prerequisite
|* for any whole-chain raw-tap-to-sampled-bit post-layout claim."
|*
|* Topology, post-layout side (prefix p): xarr is ONE flat-extracted cell,
|* sourced from layout/pex-sampler-core/sampler_core_pex.spice via
|* layout/bin/pex-netlist.py (shared, unmodified). `ro1`-`ro4` and `xo` --
|* the array's own raw taps, each already an internal net of the wrapper
|* `sampler_core_pex` (promoted there so its own six sampler_dff instances
|* can reach them, per layout/pex-sampler-core/README.md's alias table) --
|* are reachable at ONE level of hierarchy (`v(xarr.ro1)`, ...,
|* `v(xarr.xo)`), confirmed by this deck's own development probe before
|* committing (a first attempt at `v(xarr.xpex.ro1)`, guessing the
|* extractor's own internal `__core` instance name `xpex` was needed, came
|* back "not available or has zero length" -- `ro1`/`xo` belong to
|* `sampler_core_pex`'s OWN local scope, one level shallower than that).
|* `xo`'s own two-ring partial sum `t1` is NOT reached by this deck --
|* unlike sim/post-layout-ro-array-core/, which promotes `t1` at the very
|* same one-hierarchy-level depth this deck's own probe found for `ro1`/
|* `xo`, `t1` is internal to the array block nested one level deeper inside
|* `sampler_core_pex` (the array's own combining tree is not itself promoted
|* to `sampler_core_pex`'s local scope, only its four raw taps and the
|* fully-combined `xo` are) -- reaching it would need a second, unverified
|* hierarchy guess this deck does not spend budget confirming. The N=4
|* (`xo`) edge-retention/value-fidelity figures below are this deck's own
|* combining-fidelity claim; the N=2 (`t1`) figure sim/
|* post-layout-ro-array-core/ also reports is not re-measured here.
|*
|* Topology, pre-layout side (prefix-free): xctl is
|* design/sampler_core.spice's own parameterized `.subckt sampler_core`,
|* same-deck same-corner control, `ro1`-`ro4`/`xo` reached the identical way
|* (`v(xctl.ro1)`, ..., `v(xctl.xo)` -- local nets of `.subckt sampler_core`
|* itself, per that file's own `xdut ... ro_array_core` instantiation line).
|*
|* The substrate tie. layout/pex-sampler-core/sampler_core_pex.spice
|* declares the extractor's substrate return node `vsubs` .global
|* (klayout-tools#1503, same as every other post-layout deck in this repo).
|* This deck ties it HARD to 0, the same physically-motivated choice
|* sim/post-layout-ro-array-core/ and its own siblings use -- every composed
|* cell's own psub guard ring is tied to vss, and vss is 0 here.
|*
|* START-UP: ENABLE + RESET RELEASE, NOT `.ic` ON INTERNAL NODES -- same
|* method sim/post-layout-ro-array-core/'s own header explains for the
|* rings (en=0 pins each ro_nand2's own output high, a defined state;
|* releasing it starts the ring), extended here to the six sampler_dff
|* instances the SAME way: rst_n=0 pins each instance's own `mb`/`s2mid`/
|* `qb` internal nodes to a defined reset state (design/sampler_core.spice's
|* own `.subckt sampler_dff`, `Mimpb`/`Mimnb`/`Mis2pb`/`Mis2nb` -- the same
|* four devices sim/post-layout-sampler-dff/'s own reset-contention deck
|* exercises with an explicit PWL pulse), so releasing rst_n from a defined
|* state is exactly as valid a start-up method as `.ic`, and reaches deeper
|* into this deck's own hierarchy (six instances inside two more levels of
|* subckt nesting than sim/raw-bit-min-entropy/'s own top-level sampler_dff
|* calls) with no per-instance `.ic` ladder needed at all. This deck can use
|* a REAL transient rst_n pulse -- unlike sim/raw-bit-min-entropy/, which
|* holds rst_n permanently released because its own trnoise() sources
|* cannot coexist with ANY control-signal breakpoint in this ngspice build
|* -- because this deck injects no noise at all (a deterministic functional/
|* timing/current characterization, not a min-entropy campaign).
|*
|* Timeline. `en1`-`en4` release together at 5 ns (matching
|* sim/post-layout-ro-array-core/ exactly, so the rings reach the same
|* steady oscillation this deck's own ring-period/combining measurements
|* below can cite directly). `rst_n` releases at 300 ns -- comfortably past
|* every ring's own start-up transient at the periods that deck measures
|* (2-4 ns), so the reset-held window below (50-250 ns) is a fair "rings
|* running, samplers held in reset" baseline, not a start-up artifact.
|* `clk` begins pulsing at 320 ns, Ts = 100 ns (the same disclosed,
|* measured compute-budget deviation from DR-0003's Ts = 20 us that
|* sim/raw-bit-min-entropy/'s own header justifies at length -- this deck's
|* own tstop of 800 ns gives five rising clk edges, 320-720 ns, comfortably
|* inside that window). No trnoise() source anywhere in this deck, so no
|* control-signal-breakpoint conflict of the kind that forces
|* sim/raw-bit-min-entropy/ to hold every control signal at `dc`.
|*
|* What "captured value" means here, and what it does NOT claim. With no
|* injected noise, `raw_bit`/`raw_valid`/`ring_bit1`-`ring_bit4` are fully
|* deterministic functions of the free-running rings' own phase at each
|* `clk` edge -- this deck reports FIVE discrete snapshots per side (one
|* per sample instant, at the 50 ns mark inside each `clk` low phase, where
|* every sampler's own slave stage is opaque and holding) to confirm the
|* whole assembled, post-layout cell produces clean rail-to-rail digital
|* levels end to end (not an intermediate voltage, not floating) when
|* driven by its own real ring taps through its own real routing -- NOT a
|* min-entropy or jitter claim (that remains sim/raw-bit-min-entropy/'s own
|* scope, at the pre-layout netlist level only). Pre- and post-layout
|* snapshots at the SAME nominal sample instant are NOT expected to agree
|* bit-for-bit: post-layout parasitics measurably slow the array (this
|* deck's own p_tr*/tr* ratio below quantifies exactly how much), so the
|* two sides' sampler_dff instances can legitimately latch different phases
|* of each ring's own free-running waveform at the same nominal clock edge.
|* That divergence is itself the mechanism this whole entropy source
|* depends on, not a defect in either side.
|*
|* Window / memory. Without an explicit `.save`, ngspice retains a
|* full-resolution trace for every internal parasitic-star leg node this
|* flat extraction introduces (264 devices' worth, on TOP of the samplers'
|* own leg nodes) -- confirmed to exhaust available process memory outright
|* during this deck's own development (`Error: memory required ... is more
|* than memory available`), the same failure
|* sim/post-layout-ro-array-core/'s own header names for the array alone.
|* `.save` below keeps only the traces every `.meas` statement actually
|* reads.
|*
|* This file is a TEMPLATE: sim/bin/corner-run.py substitutes /home/ubuntu/.volare/volare/sky130/versions/c6d73a35f524070e85faff4a6a9eef49553ebc2b/sky130A/libs.tech/combined/sky130.lib.spice,
|* ss, -40.0, 1.62 and 5p. As committed it is not a
|* runnable deck. Invoke with `--ro-ring5 design/sampler_core.spice` and
|* `--pex-lib layout/pex-sampler-core/sampler_core_pex.spice`.
